% AutoTailor template: Jake's Resume, compact. A denser variant of Jake's Resume
% (https://github.com/jakegut/resume, MIT License, below):
% - 10pt text and 0.4in/0.5in margins, so a full page holds about twice the bullets;
% - each job's or project's tech stack after its title ("Research Intern | Python, PyTorch");
% - leadership entries on two lines (title, group and dates; then what you did);
% - education details with a bold label ("Coursework: ...");
% - one skills row per group.
% The two pdfTeX-only Unicode lines are guarded (\ifdefined) so the file also compiles with
% Tectonic's XeTeX engine; the body is generated.
